                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> George Tobin (1768-1838),     naval officer and artist, who sailed on Bligh's second voyage to Tahiti and also sailed
    with Cochrane. He seems to have been at home on half-pay between 1801 and 1804, when he is noted in the diary.
    See entries for his brothers, primarily <persName key="TOB02">James Webbe Tobin</persName> but also <persName key="TOB01">John Tobin</persName>.</p>
                    </note>
